---
title: "Columns Tool Panel"
enterprise: true
---

The Columns Tool Panel provides controls for managing the grid's columns. Use it to show, hide and reorder columns, group rows, aggregate data and pivot.

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/screenshot.png" alt="Columns Tool Panel with the Top Area, Columns, Row Groups, Values and Column Labels (Pivot) sections labelled" centered=true constrained=true width="35rem" /%}

## Columns Tool Panel Sections

The Columns Tool Panel is split into the following sections, from top to bottom.

### Top Area

Turn [Pivot Mode](./pivoting/) on or off, expand or collapse all column groups, select or unselect all columns, and search the Columns section by column name.

### Columns Section

Lists every column available to the grid, grouped by column group. Select a column to show or hide it or, in pivot mode, to group, aggregate or pivot it. Drag a column to reorder it, to move it into a drop zone or, when enabled, onto the grid to show it.

### Drop Zones

The **Row Groups Section**, **Values Section** and **Column Labels (Pivot) Section** hold the columns used for the grid's [Row Grouping](./grouping/), [Aggregation](./aggregation/) and [Pivoting](./pivoting/).

